    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear tactical mandate: exploit the stolen base potential against pitchers with high delivery times. **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.40) stand as our primary anchors against Springs. **Trea Turner** benefits from an optimal leadoff spot and a rare convergence of favorable wind conditions and a slow opposing delivery that screams stolen base opportunity. **Kyle Schwarber** provides immense ceiling alongside him, with his 0.394 xwOBA and platoon advantage making him a premier start. Elsewhere, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.73) earns a significant boost today; while his 8th-order slot is suboptimal, his 14% platoon edge against Singer and his elite speed profile solidify his position as a high-reward asset for our SB-starved rotation.\n\nBeyond our top-tier plays, we are leaning into favorable matchups for **Hyeseong Kim** (63.54) and **Junior Caminero** (64.13). **Hyeseong Kim** is a high-upside play today because he faces McCullers Jr., whose glacial delivery time effectively guarantees the green light for our elite speedsters on the basepaths. Conversely, the benching of **Dillon Dingler** (38.75) was the most difficult decision of the morning; while he demonstrates a solid 0.374 xwOBA, his score dipped below our 40-point floor due to a severe negative platoon shift against Gray, making him a liability in our efficiency-weighted format.\n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely for any shifts that might suppress fly balls, but the current wind-out projection is working in favor of our power-heavy bats. The matchup for **Yordan Alvarez** (66.29) remains high-leverage despite the presence of an elite arm in Glasnow; his elite xwOBA of 0.428 serves as the necessary buffer to keep him in the lineup. With **Christian Yelich** remaining on the IL and **Zac Veen** still honing his craft in Albuquerque, the Zebras are relying heavily on the dynamic versatility of **Chase Meidroth** (58.06) and **Carson Benge** (59.17) to provide secondary production. We remain cautious with **Kazuma Okamoto** (56.97) and **Colt Keith** (55.37), both of whom are start-worthy but face SPs with decent xERAs, requiring them to rely on their respective order positions to maintain value throughout the day.",
